Cohort Definition:
Index Event: First date on which both a diagnosis of heart failure and a diagnosis of end-stage renal disease are recorded on the same day (first co-occurrence).
Inclusion Criteria: History of heart failure any time before the index date (prior diagnosis of heart failure at any time before the index event)., Diagnosis of end-stage renal disease on the index date as part of the co-occurrence., Adults aged 18 years or older at the index date (age >= 18).
Observation Window: Follow-up from index until end of continuous observation (end of enrollment) or death; no fixed follow-up duration.
Prior Observation: No prior observation or continuous enrollment requirement before index.
Cohort Exit: Exit cohort at end of continuous observation (end of enrollment) or at death.

[Step 1] Decomposing cohort definition into concept sets...

✅ Decomposed into 4 concept sets:
  1. Heart failure (Condition, SNOMED) (Condition)
     Intent: All diagnoses indicating heart failure to identify prior history (used for the requirement: prior diagnosis of heart failure any time before the index date and for the co-occurrence on index date). Include acute, chronic, systolic/diastolic, left ventricular failure, and cardiomyopathy with heart failure.
     Queries: heart failure, congestive heart failure, congestive cardiac failure...
  2. End-stage renal disease (ESRD) / CKD stage 5 (Condition, SNOMED) (Condition)
     Intent: All diagnoses indicating end-stage renal disease, end-stage kidney disease, CKD stage 5, dialysis-dependent renal failure — to be used to define the ESRD diagnosis that must co-occur on the index date.
     Queries: end stage renal disease, end-stage kidney disease, ESRD...
  3. Dialysis procedures (supporting) - Hemodialysis and Peritoneal dialysis (Procedure: SNOMED, CPT4) (Procedure)
     Intent: Procedure concepts indicating maintenance dialysis (hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis). This supporting set can help capture patients with ESRD when diagnosis coding is inconsistent. Use for sensitivity analyses or to supplement identification of dialysis-dependent ESRD on index date.
     Queries: hemodialysis, haemodialysis, maintenance hemodialysis...
  4. Chronic kidney disease unspecified / kidney failure (supporting broader CKD concepts) (Condition, SNOMED) (Condition)
     Intent: Broader CKD and kidney failure diagnoses to support sensitivity analyses for ESRD identification (e.g., 'chronic kidney disease' and 'kidney failure' terms that may be coded when stage is not specified). Use with caution and only in sensitivity analyses or to help find candidate concepts for the ESRD set.
     Queries: chronic kidney disease, kidney failure, renal failure chronic...

